WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.101 --> 00:00:06.774
"You look hungry and tired," the prince said to Tom.

2
00:00:06.775 --> 00:00:08.404
"Come with me."

3
00:00:08.405 --> 00:00:12.929
Tom was stunned by what was happening.

4
00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:19.998
The prince led him through the palace until they came to the prince's room.

5
00:00:19.999 --> 00:00:25.503
While the prince ordered breakfast for his guest, Tom looked around.

6
00:00:25.504 --> 00:00:31.491
"Imagine sleeping in that big bed instead of on the floor!" Tom thought.

7
00:00:31.492 --> 00:00:38.349
"He has so many books and a suit of armor and—"

8
00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:41.384
"What's your name and where do you live?"

9
00:00:41.385 --> 00:00:44.507
The prince interrupted Tom's thoughts.

10
00:00:44.508 --> 00:00:50.156
"I'm Tom Canty from Offal Street. And who are you?"

11
00:00:50.157 --> 00:00:53.873
"Prince Edward."

12
00:00:53.874 --> 00:01:00.384
"Prince Edward! You mean, King Henry's son and heir?"

13
00:01:00.385 --> 00:01:05.130
The prince nodded, and Tom quickly bowed.

14
00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:07.916
"I'm sorry to hear that the king is ill.

15
00:01:07.917 --> 00:01:11.538
Everyone is talking about him.”

16
00:01:11.539 --> 00:01:14.978
"I fear that my father may die soon.

17
00:01:14.979 --> 00:01:20.420
Some people say he's cruel, but he has always treated me fairly."

18
00:01:20.421 --> 00:01:22.909
The prince paused and smiled.

19
00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:26.265
"Though he does like to criticize me."

20
00:01:26.266 --> 00:01:30.907
"My father is mean to everyone!" Tom said.

21
00:01:30.908 --> 00:01:39.356
Just then Tom's meal arrived, and he dug in with both hands.

22
00:01:39.357 --> 00:01:45.504
"He has no table manners," Prince Edward thought, "and yet . . ."

23
00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:51.219
"You speak as though you've had some education," the prince said to Tom.

24
00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:55.878
"Yes, I can read and write, but I struggle with Latin."

25
00:01:55.879 --> 00:01:59.944
"Latin is hard at first," the prince said.

26
00:01:59.945 --> 00:02:06.483
"But enough about studying. Is it pleasant to live on Offal Street?"

27
00:02:06.484 --> 00:02:11.844
Tom thought about the poor families who crowded together in every house.

28
00:02:11.845 --> 00:02:16.422
"Sometimes it is, but not when we're hungry."

29
00:02:16.423 --> 00:02:19.853
He gobbled up some ham and eggs.

30
00:02:19.854 --> 00:02:22.928
"I hope that doesn't happen too often.

31
00:02:22.929 --> 00:02:27.200
Do you have any friends? What do you like to do?"

32
00:02:27.201 --> 00:02:29.786
Tom swallowed some bread.

33
00:02:29.787 --> 00:02:34.066
"My friends and I are always racing to see who's the fastest."

34
00:02:34.067 --> 00:02:38.017
"Oh, I'd like that!" the prince said.

35
00:02:38.018 --> 00:02:43.198
"People say I'm a good runner, but I don't have anyone to compete against.

36
00:02:43.199 --> 00:02:49.813
My only friends are my older sister, Princess Elizabeth, and my cousin, Lady Jane.

37
00:02:49.814 --> 00:02:53.233
What else do you do with your friends?"

38
00:02:53.234 --> 00:02:55.926
"In summer we swim in the river.

39
00:02:55.927 --> 00:02:59.184
We shout and splash each other with water.

40
00:02:59.185 --> 00:03:06.851
Of course, that's after we've played in the mud and made mud pies!"

41
00:03:06.852 --> 00:03:11.845
"I'm not allowed to get wet outdoors," the prince said sadly.

42
00:03:11.846 --> 00:03:16.355
"Then how do you get clean?" Tom asked.

43
00:03:16.356 --> 00:03:19.695
"I have many servants who help me bathe."

44
00:03:19.696 --> 00:03:23.237
The prince sighed.

45
00:03:23.238 --> 00:03:26.437
"Your life sounds wonderful.

46
00:03:26.438 --> 00:03:32.800
If I could run barefoot in the mud, I'd give up my right to be king!"

47
00:03:32.801 --> 00:03:35.026
Tom was horrified.

48
00:03:35.027 --> 00:03:40.199
"You can't do that, sir! Besides, it's not all fun.

49
00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:46.046
On New Year's Day, my best friend, Julian, fell into the river and almost drowned.

50
00:03:46.047 --> 00:03:49.815
Luckily, a stranger saved him."

51
00:03:49.816 --> 00:03:55.704
"I'm sorry to hear about Julian, but I wish I could play with your friends."

52
00:03:55.705 --> 00:04:02.852
"And I wish I could be a prince, if only for one day."

53
00:04:02.853 --> 00:04:07.300
"Would you really like that?" the prince asked.

54
00:04:07.301 --> 00:04:10.917
Tom nodded.

55
00:04:10.918 --> 00:04:13.026
Prince Edward grinned.

56
00:04:13.027 --> 00:04:15.686
"Then let's do it!

57
00:04:15.687 --> 00:04:23.178
We'll trade clothes for a while and then switch back before anyone finds out."

58
00:04:23.179 --> 00:04:31.573
A few minutes later, the prince was wearing Tom's rags, and Tom was dressed in the prince's fine garments.

59
00:04:31.574 --> 00:04:35.765
The two boys stood side by side in front of a large mirror.

60
00:04:35.766 --> 00:04:41.600
They stared at each other, then at the mirror, then at each other again.

61
00:04:41.601 --> 00:04:45.384
"We look so much alike," Edward whispered.

62
00:04:45.385 --> 00:04:52.903
Tom laughed nervously. "We do indeed, sir."

63
00:04:52.904 --> 00:04:59.080
"Except . . ." Edward frowned, peering at Tom's hand.

64
00:04:59.081 --> 00:05:03.559
"You have a bruise where that guard grabbed your hand."

65
00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:07.919
"It's nothing." Tom hid his hand behind his back.

66
00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:13.641
"It was cruel!" The prince stamped his foot.

67
00:05:13.642 --> 00:05:15.926
"Now close your eyes.

68
00:05:15.927 --> 00:05:21.768
I need to put away something important before I leave."

69
00:05:21.769 --> 00:05:23.727
Tom didn't peek.

70
00:05:23.728 --> 00:05:30.924
He imagined that Edward was hiding documents—or even jewels.

71
00:05:30.925 --> 00:05:33.831
"All done!" Edward said.

72
00:05:33.832 --> 00:05:39.627
"Don't move until I return to this room. That's a command!"

73
00:05:39.628 --> 00:05:45.970
Tom stood still while Edward rushed from the room and out to the courtyard.

74
00:05:45.971 --> 00:05:50.893
"Open this gate at once!" Edward shouted to the guard.

75
00:05:50.894 --> 00:05:53.601
The guard hurried to open the gate.

76
00:05:53.602 --> 00:05:58.411
But as Edward passed by, the guard knocked him to the ground.

77
00:05:58.412 --> 00:06:05.144
"You wretched pauper! Because of you, I got a scolding from Prince Edward!"

78
00:06:05.145 --> 00:06:10.466
Edward's face flushed with anger as he picked himself up.

79
00:06:10.467 --> 00:06:12.585
"I'm Prince Edward!

80
00:06:12.586 --> 00:06:18.587
When I return, you'll be locked up for hurting me—and my friend!"

81
00:06:18.588 --> 00:06:22.760
The guard sneered and gave Edward a mock salute.

82
00:06:22.761 --> 00:06:27.288
"I salute Your Gracious Highness.

83
00:06:27.289 --> 00:06:29.991
Now get out of here!"

84
00:06:29.992 --> 00:06:35.354
A few people were still waiting outside the gate, hoping for a glimpse of royalty.

85
00:06:35.355 --> 00:06:41.397
They laughed and shouted.

86
00:06:41.398 --> 00:06:48.441
"Make way for His Royal Highness!" they cried.

